kdriver: PCIe device node mode is hex 0x0666, meant octal 0666

Re-applied at build time to the pinned mx3_driver_pub tag (v2.1.0; still present on
v2.2.0 and the release branch). kdriver/linux/pcie/memx_pcie.h defines
DEVICE_NODE_DEFAULT_ACCESS_RIGHT as (0x0666), which memx_pcie_devnode() hands to
the kernel as the node mode. 0x0666 is 0o3146, so /dev/memx0 and
/dev/memx0_feature are created as c--xr-SrwT (setgid + sticky, owner exec only)
instead of crw-rw-rw-. The USB header already uses the octal (0666). The sysext
udev rule (MODE="0666") does not correct it, confirmed on TrueNAS 26.0.0-BETA.3
hardware before and after a reboot. Privileged Frigate is unaffected (root), but
anything relying on the documented 0666 is not.

No functional change beyond the node mode; no driver version change. Fixed in both
the kdriver/ and 32bit_driver/ copies. The applier skips this once it lands in the
pinned tag.

diff --git a/32bit_driver/kdriver/linux/pcie/memx_pcie.h b/32bit_driver/kdriver/linux/pcie/memx_pcie.h
index 9a8c2a3..8c71a12 100644
--- a/32bit_driver/kdriver/linux/pcie/memx_pcie.h
+++ b/32bit_driver/kdriver/linux/pcie/memx_pcie.h
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
 #define PCIE_NAME "memx_pcie_ai_chip"
 
 #define DEVICE_NODE_NAME "memx%d"
-#define DEVICE_NODE_DEFAULT_ACCESS_RIGHT (0x0666)
+#define DEVICE_NODE_DEFAULT_ACCESS_RIGHT (0666)
 #define DEVICE_CLASS_NAME "memx_cdev"
 
 #define MEMX_PCIE_VENDOR_ID (0x1FE9)
diff --git a/kdriver/linux/pcie/memx_pcie.h b/kdriver/linux/pcie/memx_pcie.h
index 8920272..c6abcab 100644
--- a/kdriver/linux/pcie/memx_pcie.h
+++ b/kdriver/linux/pcie/memx_pcie.h
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
 #define PCIE_NAME "memx_pcie_ai_chip"
 
 #define DEVICE_NODE_NAME "memx%d"
-#define DEVICE_NODE_DEFAULT_ACCESS_RIGHT (0x0666)
+#define DEVICE_NODE_DEFAULT_ACCESS_RIGHT (0666)
 #define DEVICE_CLASS_NAME "memx_cdev"
 
 #define MEMX_PCIE_VENDOR_ID (0x1FE9)
